// Because the body of the 200 is an array of this schema, a value outside this enum makes the WHOLE response non-conforming, not just the one row — one operator `INSERT`, one writer added without a contract change, or one restored backup, and a validating consumer rejects six good rows along with the odd one. That is the intended alarm in a test and the wrong behaviour in a UI, so the expected handling is stated rather than left to each consumer: coerce an unrecognised value to `unknown` and render the row, as the shipped client already does (smart-calendar-flow/src/api/client.ts:435), instead of discarding the response. Factory §4 mandates a generated zod `schemas.ts` in the frontend, which is where this would otherwise bite.
//
// It names WHAT happened, not WHO did it. Every entry's subject is the calling user (see the operation description); no entry carries an actor, and no value in this enum distinguishes an action a person took from one the scheduler took on their behalf.
type AuditEntryAction string

